{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++ code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++ code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include<cstdio>\n#include<iostream>\nusing namespace std;\ntypedef long long ll;\nconst int MOD = 1000000007;\n\nstruct Matrix {\n    int mat[33][33];\n} identity, base[70], result, prefix[70], suffix[70];\n\nll n, k;\n\nvoid printMatrix(Matrix m) {\n    for (int i = 0; i <= k; ++i) {\n        for (int j = 0; j <= k; ++j)\n            cout << m.mat[i][j] << ' ';\n        cout << '\\n';\n    }\n    cout << '\\n';\n}\n\nMatrix multiply(Matrix a, Matrix b) {\n    Matrix c = identity;\n    for (int k_idx = 0; k_idx <= k; ++k_idx) {\n        for (int i = 0; i <= k; ++i) {\n            for (int j = 0; j <= k; ++j) {\n                ll temp = (static_cast<ll>(a.mat[i][k_idx]) * b.mat[k_idx][j]) % MOD;\n                c.mat[i][j] = (c.mat[i][j] + temp) % MOD;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    return c;\n}\n\nvoid preprocess() {\n    prefix[0] = base[0];\n    for (int i = 1; i < k; ++i)\n        prefix[i] = multiply(prefix[i-1], base[i]);\n    \n    suffix[k-1] = base[k-1];\n    for (int i = k-2; i >= 0; --i)\n        suffix[i] = multiply(base[i], suffix[i+1]);\n    \n    base[0] = suffix[0];\n    for (int i = 1; i < k; ++i)\n        base[i] = multiply(suffix[i], prefix[i-1]);\n}\n\nvoid solve() {\n    cin >> n >> k;\n    int i, j;\n    result = identity;\n    for (i = 0; i < k; ++i) {\n        base[i] = identity;\n        for (j = 0; j <= k; ++j)\n            base[i].mat[j][j] = 1;\n        for (j = 0; j <= k; ++j)\n            base[i].mat[j][i] = 1;\n        result.mat[i][i] = 1;\n    }\n    result.mat[k][k] = 1;\n    \n    for (; n > 0; n /= k) {\n        int digit = n % k;\n        if (digit) {\n            ll pos = 0, temp = n;\n            while (temp) {\n                pos = (pos + (temp /= k)) % k;\n            }\n            for (i = digit - 1; i >= 0; --i) {\n                result = multiply(base[(pos + i) % k], result);\n            }\n        }\n        preprocess();\n    }\n    \n    int answer = 1;\n    for (i = 0; i < k; ++i)\n        answer = (answer + result.mat[k][i]) % MOD;\n    cout << answer << '\\n';\n}\n\nint main() {\n    solve();\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport sys\n\nMOD = 1000000007\n\nclass Matrix:\n    def __init__(self, size=33):\n        self.mat = [[0] * size for _ in range(size)]\n    \n    def copy(self):\n        new_mat = Matrix()\n        for i in range(len(self.mat)):\n            for j in range(len(self.mat[i])):\n                new_mat.mat[i][j] = self.mat[i][j]\n        return new_mat\n\ndef multiply(a, b, k):\n    c = Matrix()\n    # Initialize as identity matrix\n    for i in range(k + 1):\n        for j in range(k + 1):\n            c.mat[i][j] = 1 if i == j else 0\n    \n    for k_idx in range(k + 1):\n        for i in range(k + 1):\n            for j in range(k + 1):\n                temp = (a.mat[i][k_idx] * b.mat[k_idx][j]) % MOD\n                c.mat[i][j] = (c.mat[i][j] + temp) % MOD\n    return c\n\ndef preprocess(prefix, suffix, base, k):\n    prefix[0] = base[0].copy()\n    for i in range(1, k):\n        prefix[i] = multiply(prefix[i-1], base[i], k)\n    \n    suffix[k-1] = base[k-1].copy()\n    for i in range(k-2, -1, -1):\n        suffix[i] = multiply(base[i], suffix[i+1], k)\n    \n    base[0] = suffix[0].copy()\n    for i in range(1, k):\n        base[i] = multiply(suffix[i], prefix[i-1], k)\n\ndef solve():\n    data = sys.stdin.readline().strip().split()\n    n = int(data[0])\n    k = int(data[1])\n    \n    # Initialize matrices\n    identity = Matrix()\n    for i in range(k + 1):\n        identity.mat[i][i] = 1\n    \n    base = [Matrix() for _ in range(70)]\n    prefix = [Matrix() for _ in range(70)]\n    suffix = [Matrix() for _ in range(70)]\n    result = Matrix()\n    \n    # Initialize result as identity matrix\n    for i in range(k + 1):\n        result.mat[i][i] = 1\n    \n    # Initialize base matrices\n    for i in range(k):\n        base[i] = identity.copy()\n        for j in range(k + 1):\n            base[i].mat[j][j] = 1\n        for j in range(k + 1):\n            base[i].mat[j][i] = 1\n    \n    while n > 0:\n        digit = n % k\n        if digit:\n            pos = 0\n            temp = n\n            while temp:\n                temp //= k\n                pos = (pos + temp) % k\n            \n            for i in range(digit - 1, -1, -1):\n                result = multiply(base[(pos + i) % k], result, k)\n        \n        preprocess(prefix, suffix, base, k)\n        n //= k\n    \n    answer = 1\n    for i in range(k):\n        answer = (answer + result.mat[k][i]) % MOD\n    print(answer)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    solve()\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.75\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.00013350549852475524, -5.960462772236497e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.19011150300502777, -0.00018690270371735096, -0.0004926898400299251, -0.00142020417843014, 0.0, -2.3841855067985307e-07, 0.0, -3.576278118089249e-07, -0.0001591317413840443, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07